+## Held biome swipes and duplicate input (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements **R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01**. The owner describes a long swipe, stationary stop, release and immediate jump to the original page; they confirmed it starts in the **Create biome area**. This is reproduced through Godot's full input pipeline, not a threshold failure. A touch generates an emulated mouse event **before** the original touch is dispatched. During a page swipe, the starting biome button moves with the finger. The earlier mouse UP selects that button and `_preview_creation_biome` rebuilds Create, destroying its swipe handler before the subsequent ScreenTouch UP. A stationary hold makes this particularly easy because the button is exactly under the resting finger.
+
+Engine ordering and emulation identity are supported by the [Godot 4.7 input implementation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.7/core/input/input.cpp#L836) and [InputEvent documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/classes/class_inputevent.html#class-inputevent-constant-device-id-emulation). The observed rebuild/activation is directly reproduced by local tests. The older `Viewport.push_input` fixtures bypassed this engine emulation path; their passing movement tests therefore missed this phone failure.
+
+`game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` now intercepts **only** emulated mouse events for touches owned by page navigation. The first emulated press settles an arriving page before the same ownership hit-test; emulated motion/release for an active page gesture is consumed. The actual touch handles the swipe or one deliberate tap. Carousel, ranges, text fields, press-action buttons and modals retain their input, and real desktop mouse events remain available. No additional sensitivity/easing adjustment, global emulation setting, physics, account or backend change. Current 20-unit commitment, six-unit relaxation boundary, fixed header, adjacent content, gutter, gentle failed return and end spring retain their behavior.
+
+Changed files for this task: `game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` (the new emulated-event branch), `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd` (full engine routing regression), this document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md` and `docs/evidence/held-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/`. Concurrent cached-page mouse-behavior corrections in the handler/app were preserved; the scoped patch excludes those independent edits. No mixed-workspace commit.
